Place-n-Time, Dapper Mapper's newest map viewer for Linux, provides a
handy way to navigate through maps drawn from freely available data
provided by the United States Geological Survey (USGS).  Place-n-Time is
aimed at users who enjoy working with topographic maps: hikers, canoeists,
bicyclists, historians, or anyone else who wants to look closely at a
small corner of the planet.  It may also be used to view overlay maps
created by users of Dapper Mapper's XViewSDTS.

For more information or to download a free beta-test version of
Place-n-Time, go to http://www.dappermapper.com/products/placentime/beta/

